From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 04:37:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/vf_hqdn3d_cuda: add a CUDA hqdn3d filter

Add hqdn3d_cuda, a CUDA port of the integer hqdn3d filter whose output
is identical to the CPU filter. It takes the options and commands of
hqdn3d and uses the shared tables in hqdn3d_coefs.c.

A horizontal kernel filters each row into an intermediate buffer; a
vertical kernel filters each column and applies the temporal lowpass
against the previous output. The temporal state is dropped where
hqdn3d drops it, and after a frame size change inside a running graph
the output frames come from a frames context of the new size.

p012 is not accepted: hwupload_cuda converts it to p016, so that path
cannot be exercised.

libavfilter/tests/hqdn3d_vulkan now also runs the CUDA filter with a
cuda:<index> argument, and builds when only one of the two GPU filters
is enabled.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
