+@anchor{hqdn3d_cuda}
+@section hqdn3d_cuda
+
+Apply a High Quality 3D Denoiser using CUDA.
+The output is bit-exact to the CPU @ref{hqdn3d} filter. The one exception is
+@samp{p010}: where the CPU filter writes a value above the format maximum,
+which this format cannot store, this filter writes the format maximum.
+
+Supported input hardware frame software formats:
+@itemize
+@item @samp{yuv420p}
+@item @samp{yuv422p}
+@item @samp{yuv444p}
+@item @samp{yuv420p10}
+@item @samp{yuv444p10}
+@item @samp{yuv444p16}
+@item @samp{nv12}
+@item @samp{p010}
+@item @samp{p016}
+@end itemize
+
+The filter accepts the same options as @ref{hqdn3d}:
+@table @option
+@item luma_spatial
+@item chroma_spatial
+@item luma_tmp
+@item chroma_tmp
+@end table
+
+@subsection Commands
+This filter supports the same @ref{commands} as options.
+
 @anchor{hqdn3d_vulkan}
 @section hqdn3d_vulkan
 
